Show that the fixed point combinator is the same as the fixed point combinator defined using a choice function.

We define the fixed point combinator \(\text{fix}\) using the following equation:
$$\text{fix} f = f (\text{fix} f)$$

We define the fixed point combinator \(\text{fixC}\) using a choice function \(C\) as follows:
$$\text{fixC} f = (C \circ f) \circ f$$

We can prove that these two fixed point combinators are equivalent using the following steps:
\begin{align*}
\text{fixC} f & = (C \circ f) \circ f \\
& = (C \circ f) \circ (C \circ f) \circ f \\
& = (C \circ f) \circ (C \circ f) \circ (C \circ f) \circ f \\
& = \ldots \\
& = \text{fix} f
\end{align*}

