Let $f$ be a function. The update function $f[i \leftarrow x]$ is defined by $f[i \leftarrow x](i) = x$ and $f[i \leftarrow x](j) = f(j)$ for $j \neq i$. The inverse of a function $g$ is a function $g^{-1}$ such that $g^{-1} \circ g = \text{id}$.  We want to show that $(f[i \leftarrow x])^{-1} = f[i \leftarrow x^{-1}]$.

Let $j$ be any element of the domain of $f$. Then
